 "_doc": "World 3 and World 4 monster frames (enemies3.py): 128-unit frames, 2 units = 1 world px, facing right. Each kind has one anchor (its feet, or its middle). Offsets from the anchor in world px = (point - anchor) / 2 (elites.frame_point). eyes = the list of the lit eyes' points ([[x, y]] for one); eye1 and eye2 (or eye) name them; eye_mid = the middle of two; eye_r = an eye's radius; hit = [x, y, w, h], the body's box on that frame.",
